@scene(100)

// INTERFACES FIRST: a base with a lid bolted on, a cover screwed flush, and a
// slider running in a guide, designed from the places the parts meet.
//
// PARTS MEET AT INTERFACES, AND FASTENERS ARE INSERTED INTO THEM. Each
// interface is declared once, before any part, as one value:
//
//   - the DECK, the face the lid and the cover sit on (joint.planarFace);
//   - the GUIDE, the channel the slider runs in (joint.prismatic);
//   - four AXES, the screws' (joint.cylindrical): two M6 under the lid and
//     two M3 under the cover.
//
// Then every part is built from them. The base is everything below the deck
// with the guide's channel cut from it; the lid and the cover are what of
// their blanks lies above the deck; the slider is its blank bounded by the
// guide's envelope, so it fits the channel with the guide's clearance all
// round. A screw is INSERTED into an axis with joint.insert, which returns the
// screw and the parts it joins with every matching feature cut: a counterbore
// for a socket head, a flush countersink for a flat head, the ISO 273
// clearance, and the tapped hole, the screw's length picked from the grip.
//
// Moving an interface moves every part that meets there. Change an axis's
// size, or swap joint.socketHead for joint.flatHead, and the screw, its
// pocket and its tapped hole change together; nothing is kept in step by
// hand.
//
// PROVE IT WITH verifyJoints, or from the command line:
//
//   gsl joints -doc "Interface Joints.gsl"
//
// finds the four inserted screws and proves each one's fit and context: the
// screw clears the part it clamps, threads only where it engages, the
// clamped part holds the head, the base holds 1.5 d of thread with a wall
// round it, and the screw clears everything else returned.

aluminumMat, aluminumColor = metal.aluminum();

// THE INTERFACES.
deck = joint.planarFace([0.0, 0.0, 0.0], vector.dirZ);
guide = joint.prismatic([0.0, 0.0, -4.0], vector.dirX, vector.dirZ, 10.0, 6.0, 0.3);
lidAxis1 = joint.cylindrical([-20.0, 12.0, 7.5], neg(vector.dirZ), 6.0, fastener.fitMedium);
lidAxis2 = joint.cylindrical([-20.0, -12.0, 7.5], neg(vector.dirZ), 6.0, fastener.fitMedium);
coverAxis1 = joint.cylindrical([30.0, 13.0, 3.0], neg(vector.dirZ), 3.0, fastener.fitMedium);
coverAxis2 = joint.cylindrical([30.0, -13.0, 3.0], neg(vector.dirZ), 3.0, fastener.fitMedium);

// THE PARTS' BLANKS, bounded by the interfaces they meet. The lid's
// counterbores take the M6 heads from its seats at z = 7.5 to its top at 14;
// the cover is 3 thick, its flat heads flush in its top face.
baseBlank = max(box([-40.0, -20.0, -25.0], [40.0, 20.0, 0.0]), joint.below(deck),
                neg(joint.channel(guide)));
lidBlank = max(box([-38.0, -18.0, 0.0], [-2.0, 18.0, 14.0]), joint.above(deck));
coverBlank = max(box([2.0, -18.0, 0.0], [38.0, 18.0, 3.0]), joint.above(deck));
slider = max(box([25.0, -8.0, -10.0], [55.0, 8.0, 2.0]), joint.envelope(guide));

// THE SCREWS, inserted into their axes and chained through the base.
lidGrip = 7.5;
coverGrip = 3.0;
lidScrew1, lid1, base1 = joint.insert(lidAxis1, joint.socketHead, lidBlank, baseBlank, lidGrip);
lidScrew2, lid, base2 = joint.insert(lidAxis2, joint.socketHead, lid1, base1, lidGrip);
coverScrew1, cover1, base3 = joint.insert(coverAxis1, joint.flatHead, coverBlank, base2, coverGrip);
coverScrew2, cover, base = joint.insert(coverAxis2, joint.flatHead, cover1, base3, coverGrip);

lid.material = aluminumMat;
lid.color = aluminumColor;
cover.material = aluminumMat;
cover.color = aluminumColor;
slider.color = [0.15, 0.35, 0.65];

return base, lid, cover, slider, lidScrew1, lidScrew2, coverScrew1, coverScrew2;
